✅ Pull Request Title

✨ Add custom hook to detect online/offline status and display offline message


⸻

✅ PR Description

📌 Summary

This PR introduces a custom React Hook named useOnlineStatus to detect the user’s internet connectivity status. If the user goes offline, the application displays a message prompting them to check their internet connection. This improves the user experience by gracefully handling network issues.

🛠️ What’s Included
	•	Created useOnlineStatus custom hook using the navigator.onLine API and window event listeners.
	•	Integrated the hook into the Body component to conditionally show an offline message when there’s no internet connection.

⸻

✅ Why This Change
	•	Users should be informed when they lose internet access so they know why the content isn’t loading.
	•	Helps avoid confusion and enhances the reliability of the UI.
	•	Prepares the app for better offline handling in the future.

⸻

✅ How It Works (for beginners)

🧩 useOnlineStatus Hook

import { useEffect, useState } from "react";

const useOnlineStatus = () => {
  const [onlineStatus, setOnlineStatus] = useState(navigator.onLine);

  useEffect(() => {
    const handleOnline = () => setOnlineStatus(true);
    const handleOffline = () => setOnlineStatus(false);

    window.addEventListener("online", handleOnline);
    window.addEventListener("offline", handleOffline);

    return () => {
      window.removeEventListener("online", handleOnline);
      window.removeEventListener("offline", handleOffline);
    };
  }, []);

  return onlineStatus;
};

export default useOnlineStatus;

📘 Explanation:
	•	navigator.onLine tells us the current internet status (true or false).
	•	We use useState to store and reactively update the onlineStatus.
	•	window.addEventListener("online"/"offline", ...) listens for changes in network.
	•	We clean up the listeners when the component unmounts using the return function inside useEffect.

⸻

📦 Integration in Body Component

const onlineStatus = useOnlineStatus();

if (onlineStatus === false) {
  return <h1>Please check your internet connection</h1>;
}

📘 Explanation:
	•	We use the hook like any other variable.
	•	If the status is offline (false), we return a message instead of rendering the main content.
	•	This prevents errors or confusion when data can’t be fetched due to no internet.

⸻

✅ How to Test
	1.	Start the app.
	2.	Open DevTools → Network → Set to “Offline”.
	3.	You’ll see a message: “Please check your internet connection.”
	4.	Go back “Online” → The app resumes normal behavior.

